A turn on spare time runs on while a thread with time waits for the core,
so a thread that has time waits for the timer behind one that runs on what nobody wanted.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a turn on spare time runs while a thread with time waits
Witness: fuzz lend-lender-earns

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -1373,7 +1373,7 @@ static __attribute__((noinline)) void spare_look(struct core *core)
 {
     bool marked = core->run_stale;
     core->run_stale = false;
-    if ((marked && deadline_due(core)) || (core->run_queue != 0 && sched_spare_turn(core)) ||
+    if ((marked && deadline_due(core)) ||
         (marked && !turn_may_run(core))) {
         sched_turn_end();
     }
